  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;THOMAS RICH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thomas Rich was a British politician and naval officer who served as a Member of Parliament and held the rank of Admiral in the Royal Navy. He was born in 1733 and died in 1803."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL NAVY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Royal Navy is the senior branch of the British Armed Forces, where Thomas Rich served and rose through the ranks to become an Admiral."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT (MP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Member of Parliament (MP) is a political position that Thomas Rich held, representing the constituency of Sandwich from 1784 to 1790."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SANDWICH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sandwich is the constituency represented by Thomas Rich as a Member of Parliament from 1784 to 1790."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REAR-ADMIRAL OF THE BLUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RANK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rear-Admiral of the Blue is a naval rank that Thomas Rich achieved in 1794, indicating a significant promotion within the Royal Navy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VICE-ADMIRAL OF THE RED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RANK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vice-Admiral of the Red is a higher naval rank that Thomas Rich attained in 1799, further demonstrating his leadership and service."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADMIRAL OF THE BLUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RANK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Admiral of the Blue is the highest rank in the Royal Navy that Thomas Rich achieved in 1801, signifying his ultimate success and dedication."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHIEF OF ARTILLERY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RANK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chief of Artillery is a military rank that Thomas Rich held during his service in the British Army, particularly during the American Revolutionary War."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chief of Artistry is a military rank that Thomas Rich held during his service in the British Army, particularly during the American Revolutionary War."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH ARMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British Army is the land-based branch of the British Armed Forces, where Thomas Rich served as Chief of Artillery."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEVEN YEARS' WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Seven Years' War is a significant military conflict in which Thomas Rich participated, notably in the Battle of Quebec in 1759."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BATTLE OF QUEBEC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Battle of Quebec is a notable military engagement during the Seven Years' War, where Thomas Rich demonstrated bravery and tactical acumen."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN REVOLUTIONARY WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The American Revolutionary War is a major conflict in which Thomas Rich served as Chief of Artillery, playing a crucial role in the Battle of Bunker Hill."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WINDSOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Windsor is the constituency represented by Thomas Rich as a Member of Parliament from 1784 until his death in 1803."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETON COLLEGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eton College is the prestigious school where Thomas Rich received his early education, demonstrating his academic prowess."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0351</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRIST CHURCH, OXFORD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Christ Church, Oxford is the university where Thomas Rich studied military tactics and strategy after receiving his early education at Eton College."</data>
